+# PCAP Capture for prplMesh Broker Messages
+
+## Overview
+
+This feature enables capturing IEEE 1905.1 CMDU messages exchanged over the prplMesh broker (Unix Domain Socket) to a PCAP file for analysis with Wireshark.
+
+## Why This Feature?
+
+When the controller and agent run on the same device (local agent configuration), their communication happens over a Unix Domain Socket via the broker, not over network interfaces like `br-lan`. Standard packet capture tools like `tcpdump` cannot capture Unix Domain Socket traffic. This feature solves that problem by logging all broker messages to a PCAP file with proper Ethernet framing.
+
+## Usage
+
+### Enable PCAP Capture
+
+Set the `PRPLMESH_PCAP_FILE` environment variable before starting prplMesh services:
+
+```bash
+export PRPLMESH_PCAP_FILE=/tmp/prplmesh_broker.pcap
+```
+
+Then start the prplMesh services as usual. All CMDU messages (both TX and RX) will be captured to the specified file.
+
+### Analyze with Wireshark
+
+1. Copy the PCAP file to your analysis machine
+2. Open with Wireshark
+3. Apply display filters:
+
+```
+# Show all IEEE 1905.1 messages
+eth.type == 0x893a
+
+# Show only WSC M1/M2 messages (AP Autoconfiguration)
+wfa_map.message_type == 0x8002
+
+# Show specific message types
+wfa_map.tlv.type == 0x0f  # AP Radio Basic Capabilities
+wfa_map.tlv.type == 0x06  # Supported Service
+```
+
+## Implementation Details
+
+### Capture Points
+
+Messages are captured at two points in the transport layer:
+
+1. **TX Path** (`handle_broker_cmdu_tx_message`): Captures outgoing messages before they are processed
+2. (Not implemented) **RX Path** (`send_packet_to_broker`): Captures incoming messages before they are published to the broker
+
+### Packet Format
+
+Each captured packet includes:
+- **Ethernet Header** (14 bytes):
+  - Destination MAC (6 bytes)
+  - Source MAC (6 bytes)
+  - EtherType: 0x893a (IEEE 1905.1)
+- **IEEE 1905.1 CMDU Payload**: The actual message data
+
+### Key Functions
+
+- `init_pcap_capture()`: Initializes libpcap and opens the dump file
+- `write_to_pcap()`: Writes a message to the PCAP file with Ethernet framing
+- `close_pcap_capture()`: Closes the PCAP file and cleans up resources
+
+## Message Types Captured
+
+All IEEE 1905.1 CMDU messages are captured, including:
+- AP Autoconfiguration WSC (M1/M2) - Message Type 0x8002
+- Topology Discovery
+- AP Capability Query/Response
+- Client Steering
+- Channel Selection
+- And all other Multi-AP protocol messages
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### PCAP file not created
+- Ensure the directory exists and is writable
+- Check prplMesh logs for "Initializing PCAP capture" message
+- Verify `libpcap-dev` is installed in your build environment
+
+### No packets in PCAP file
+- Verify the environment variable is set before starting services
+- Check that broker communication is actually happening
+- Look for "PCAP capture initialized successfully" in logs
+
+### Build errors related to pcap
+- Try running make defconfig before package build
+- Ensure `libpcap-dev` package is installed
+- Check that CMakeLists.txt includes `pcap` in target_link_libraries
+- Verify `#include <pcap/pcap.h>` is present in ieee1905_transport.h
